  "reason": "The records collectively make the later result plausibly reconstructible. R3, R17, and R19 directly show that controlled mechanical-alloying time followed by SPS can produce homogeneous refined solid solutions and increased hardness, while R5 and R9 establish the same powder-metallurgy route and Hall–Petch/solid-solution strengthening framework. R10 supplies the specific nanocrystalline grain-boundary-hardening link, and R7, R11, R12, and R14 establish atomic-size-driven lattice distortion and substitutional solid-solution strengthening. Thus an expert could reasonably propose short-duration HEBM under argon followed by rapid vacuum SPS for an equiatomic Co-Cr-Fe-Ni-Ti alloy and predict strengthening from grain refinement, milling defects, and lattice distortion. The exact 83% FCC/17% BCC balance, Ti-specific phase-stabilization rationale, processing window, and numerical properties are not directly disclosed by the earlier records."
